# --- Godot 4 ---
godot/.godot/
godot/export_presets.cfg
*.translation

# --- Node (engine-server) ---
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

# Runtime encounter save -- regenerated by seedState()/saveState() on first run;
# not something to track in git any more than the 2D app's own browser-side
# encounter autosave is.
engine-server/state/*.json
!engine-server/state/.gitkeep

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Quaternius character assets (Phase 2) ---
# Licensed under the Quaternius Asset License v1.0 (https://quaternius.com/license.html):
# free to USE in this project, but section 3(a) prohibits redistributing the
# raw asset files themselves -- committing them to a git repo (which anyone
# who clones it could then pull back out as standalone files) risks exactly
# that, so they're kept local-only instead. Kenney's dungeon-kit is separate
# and NOT covered by this -- it's CC0 and safe to commit (see godot/assets/README.md).
godot/assets/Creatures/
godot/assets/creatures/

# --- Unused format variants from the Kenney dungeon-kit download ---
# CC0 like the rest of that pack (no license reason to exclude these) -- only
# ignored as plain repo hygiene, since this project only ever loads the GLB
# format (see GridManager.gd) and the FBX/OBJ copies + preview images are dead
# weight nobody will load. Remove this entry if you'd rather just keep everything.
godot/assets/Environment/dungeon-kit/Models/FBX format/
godot/assets/Environment/dungeon-kit/Models/OBJ format/
godot/assets/Environment/dungeon-kit/Previews/

# --- Exact duplicate of dungeon-kit above (same "Mini Dungeon (2.0)" pack,
# re-downloaded under a different folder name by mistake) -- zero new content,
# not worth tracking at all. Safe to delete this folder from disk entirely
# whenever convenient; kept out of git in the meantime.
godot/assets/Environment/kenney-dungeon/

# --- Quaternius environment MegaKits (Fantasy Props, Medieval Village,
# Stylized Nature) -- Phase 4 map-building material. Unlike the Creatures/
# packs above, these are genuinely CC0 (confirmed by reading each pack's own
# License_Standard.txt directly -- not every Quaternius pack uses the same
# license, so don't assume from the Creatures/ precedent above). Ignored here
# purely as repo hygiene, same reasoning as the Kenney FBX/OBJ entries: each
# raw download ships the same ~100-170 models in FBX/OBJ/glTF/Textures all at
# once, most of which won't end up used in any given hand-built map. Once a
# specific piece is actually used, flatten just that file into a clean path
# under godot/assets/environment/ (lowercase, mirroring creatures/hero and
# creatures/monster's own pattern) and commit that -- these three folders can
# be un-ignored instead if you'd rather just keep everything.
godot/assets/Environment/quaternius-buildings/
godot/assets/Environment/quaternius-nature/
godot/assets/Environment/quaternius-props/
